@page "/about"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About V2EN";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How V2EN translates V2EX discussions, attributes original authors, and helps readers search and ask questions about the feed.";
}
<article class="post">
    <h1>About V2EN</h1>
    <p>V2EN is an independent English-language mirror of V2EX front-page discussions about technology, software development, and everyday life. It is not affiliated with V2EX.</p>
    <h2>Where do the posts come from?</h2>
    <p>Posts come from the public V2EX feed. Each translated post links to its original source and identifies the original author and publication date. Content belongs to V2EX and the respective authors.</p>
    <h2>How accurate are the translations?</h2>
    <p>Titles and bodies are machine-translated. Translation can miss context, nuance, or technical details. Posts reflect community members' opinions, not verified reporting or advice. Use the original source to check important claims.</p>
    <h2>How often does the archive update?</h2>
    <p>The site checks the source feed periodically. New posts can remain queued while translation is in progress or provider limits apply. The home page shows the most recent fetch time; post pages show translation times when available.</p>
    <h2>How can I find a topic?</h2>
    <p><a href="/search">Keyword search</a> is free to use without an API key. <a href="/ask">Ask the feed</a> answers questions using retrieved posts and the visitor's own Google AI Studio key. AI answers can make mistakes; follow the cited posts to verify them.</p>
    <h2>How can I follow or cite V2EN?</h2>
    <p>Subscribe to the <a href="/index.xml">English Atom feed</a>. When citing a translation, include its V2EN URL, the original V2EX source, the author, and the publication date. Describe it as a machine translation.</p>
    <h2>Can AI assistants read the archive?</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/llms.txt">AI reader guide</a> describes public read-only tools and source attribution. Compatible browsers can use WebMCP to search, list recent posts, and read a translation. These tools do not require an AI provider key.</p>
</article>
